<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saqr bin Mohammed Al Qasimi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1918–<a href="/years/2010">2010</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Saqr bin Muhammad Al Qasimi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saqr bin Mohammed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> was ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> from 1948 until his death in 2010. He kept his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> out of the United Arab Emirates at its founding in December 1971, hoping for oil revenues and angered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>'s seizure of the Tunb islands, but joined it in February 1972. His more than sixty-year reign was one of the longest in the Gulf.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saqr-bin-mohammed-al-qasimi.jpg" alt="Saqr bin Mohammed Al Qasimi" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sheikh_Saqr_of_Ras_al-Khaimah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
